<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Majeerteen Sultanate</h1><p class="st-meta">1750 CE – 1927 CE (approx.) · capital Alula</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Somali sultanate of the Horn's north-eastern tip, rich from the frankincense trade, which held out against Italy until 1927.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The sultanate took shape in the mid-18th century among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majeerteen">Majeerteen</a> clan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darod">Darod</a> in the far north-east of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/somalia">Somalia</a>. Its rulers, with the title boqor (king), were based on the coast at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alula-somalia">Alula</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bargal">Bargal</a>, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-guardafui">Cape Guardafui</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The boqor ruled through clan elders, collecting revenue from frankincense, livestock and the salvage of ships wrecked on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-guardafui">Cape Guardafui</a>, which brought agreements with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> to protect crews. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boqor-osman-mahamuud">Boqor Osman Mahamuud</a> fought a long war with his kinsman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-ali-kenadid">Yusuf Ali Kenadid</a>, who left to found the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-hobyo">Sultanate of Hobyo</a>. In 1889 Osman signed a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> treaty with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Italian control remained nominal until 1925 to 1927, when Governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cesare-maria-de-vecchi">Cesare De Vecchi's</a> forces disarmed and conquered the northern sultanates and annexed them to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/italian-somaliland">Italian Somaliland</a>. The region is now part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puntland">Puntland</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/majeerteen-sultanate.jpg" alt="Majeerteen Sultanate" width="320" height="214"><figcaption>Image: 26oo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Majeerteen_sultanate_flag.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1750 CE – 1927 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Alula</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Osman Mahamuud</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Somali</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/somalia">Somalia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Migiurtinia, Majerteen Sultanate, Sultanate of Majeerteenia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1838&amp;focus=majeerteen-sultanate" aria-label="Majeerteen Sultanate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6093 1789 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Majeerteen Sultanate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6413 2045L6259 2357M6413 2045L6345 2233"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6259 2357h0M6345 2233h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6413 2045h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6413 2045h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1838&amp;focus=majeerteen-sultanate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

